% Chapter 64 of the tariff (Section XII): footwear, gaiters and the like;
% parts of such articles — all six headings (6401 to 6406) and their 25
% six-digit subheadings. A library: it includes chapter_39.le and
% section_xi.le (and through them gri.le), because Chapter 39 note 2(q) and
% Section XI note 1(n) send footwear out of those chapters, and because the
% materials of an upper or a sole are named as Chapter 39 names plastics and
% Section XI names textile materials; tariff.le includes it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 23 (2026), Chapter 64 notes 1 to 4, subheading note 1,
% Additional U.S. notes 2 and 3, and the terms of the headings and
% subheadings (https://hts.usitc.gov/); Section XII has no notes. The
% subheadings are the six-digit HS ones. The EU Combined Nomenclature
% Explanatory Notes (CN EN) to Chapter 64 say what a textile material is
% (textile flock) and where uppers of composition leather go. US Customs
% rulings name the kinds of footwear and show how the notes are read.
%
% How the chapter is read. The facts of a shoe are its kind (a boot, a
% sandal, a sneaker...), the constituent material of its upper and of its
% outer sole, and the features the subheadings name:
%   the constituent material of the upper of G is M
%       (note 4(a): the material with the greatest external surface area; or
%       "the upper of G has N percent of its external surface area of M")
%   the constituent material of the outer sole of G is M
%       (note 4(b): the material with the greatest surface in contact with
%       the ground)
%   G is designed to protect against penetration by water   (6401)
%   the upper of G is fixed to the sole by P / is assembled by P  (6401)
%   G covers the ankle;  G covers the knee
%   G incorporates a protective metal toe-cap
%   G is designed for a sporting activity; G has provision for the
%       attachment of spikes or the like   (subheading note 1)
%   G is styled as athletic footwear       (a judgment of the office:
%       Additional U.S. note 2, "tennis shoes ... and the like")
%   G has upper straps or thongs assembled to the sole by means of plugs
%   the upper of G consists of straps across the instep and around the big
%       toe
% Each material has a footwear class (note 3): rubber-plastics, leather,
% composition leather, textile or other. The heading follows from the two
% classes: 6401 and 6402 (rubber or plastics for both), 6403 (upper of
% leather), 6404 (upper of textile), 6405 (all other footwear). Heading 6406
% takes parts, removable insoles, gaiters and leggings.
% Note 1 excludes disposable coverings without applied soles, textile
% footwear without an applied outer sole, and skating boots with skates
% attached (written below). Worn footwear (6309), articles of asbestos
% (6812), orthopedic footwear (9021) and toy footwear (Chapter 95) are
% outside the model: a claim that a good belongs there is answered by the
% office (gri.le).
%
% Not modelled: the lines below six digits (value bands, the 90 percent
% rubber or plastics uppers, foxing, protective footwear, men's and women's
% sizes); "similar processes" of heading 6401 beyond the five the heading
% names.
%
% Provenance: every rule and table is labelled and cites the passage it
% encodes; the documents say where their text is (sources/), so the editor
% shows each passage and the verifier checks every quotation.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the tariff or of the rulings it
% cites, it is not a binding classification ruling, and it is not legal or
% customs advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them for a real
% import, export or declaration; consult the official texts, the customs
% authority and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no liability for
% any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a family* is a family of chapter sixty-four goods.
    *a thing* is wholly or mainly of *a material*; undefined.
    the constituent material of the upper of *a good* is *a material*; undefined.
    the upper of *a good* has *a number* percent of its external surface area of *a material*; undefined.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of *a good* is *a material*; undefined.
    *a material* is of the footwear class *a class*.
    the upper material of *a good* is *a material*.
    the upper class of *a good* is *a class*.
    the outer sole class of *a good* is *a class*.
    *a good* is designed to protect against penetration by water; undefined.
    the upper of *a good* is fixed to the sole by *a process*; undefined.
    the upper of *a good* is assembled by *a process*; undefined.
    *a process* is a process named by heading 6401.
    *a good* incorporates a protective metal toe-cap; undefined.
    *a good* covers the ankle; undefined.
    *a good* covers the knee; undefined.
    *a good* is designed for a sporting activity; undefined.
    *a good* has provision for the attachment of spikes or the like; undefined.
    *a good* is styled as athletic footwear; judged.
    *a good* has upper straps or thongs assembled to the sole by means of plugs; undefined.
    the upper of *a good* consists of straps across the instep and around the big toe; undefined.
    *a good* is a disposable covering of flimsy material without applied soles; undefined.
    *a good* is of textile material without an outer sole applied to the upper; undefined.
    *a good* has ice or roller skates attached; undefined.
    *a kind* is a kind of ski footwear.
    *a kind* is a kind of sports footwear.
    *a kind* is a kind of athletic footwear.
    *a kind* is a kind of non-athletic footwear.
    *a good* is sports footwear.
    *a good* is athletic footwear.
    the sport class of *a good* is *a class*.
    the athletic class of *a good* is *a class*.
    the height class of *a good* is *a class*.
    the toe cap of *a good* is *a cap*.
    the strap fixing of *a good* is *a fixing*.
    the upper form of *a good* is *a form*.
    the part class of *a good* is *a class*.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for sole *a sole* with upper *an upper* with sport *a sport* with fixing *a fixing* with form *a form* with cap *a cap* with height *a height* is *a code* under table footwear.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for sole *a sole* with sport *a sport* with athletic class *a class* is *a code* under table textile uppers.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for the part *a class* is *a code* under table footwear parts.

