% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: footwear, parts of footwear, gaiters and the like.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the model covers the footwear, the parts and the gaiters of Chapter 64
rule footwear_scope_family:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter sixty-four goods.

footwear is a family of chapter sixty-four goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "FOOTWEAR, GAITERS AND THE LIKE; PARTS OF SUCH ARTICLES".
footwear part is a family of chapter sixty-four goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Parts of footwear (including uppers whether or not attached to soles other than outer soles); removable insoles, heel cushions and similar articles".
gaiter is a family of chapter sixty-four goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "gaiters, leggings and similar articles, and parts thereof".

% The kinds of footwear: the tariff's own words, and the words of the
% rulings
boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N320055, confer "is a woman’s, closed toe/closed heel, tall boot".
rain boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N276145, confer "slip-on waterproof rain boot".
shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY J84976, confer "are the lace-up closure shoes that are the type traditionally worn by men".
loafer falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY J84976, confer "are also men’s shoes of the slip-on loafer type".
sneaker falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N253189, confer "over-the-ankle, lace-up sneakers".
athletic shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N253189, confer "Ryan Mid Lace athletic shoe".
sandal falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N196497, confer "is a women’s open toe/heel sandal with a rubber or plastics outer sole".
mule falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N274653, confer "slip-on, mule-type sandal".
thong sandal falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N172458, confer "is a pair of women’s open-toe/heel thong sandals".
zori falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "assembled to the sole by means of plugs (zoris)".
slipper falls in the family footwear, as stated in ruling NY N302745, confer "is a closed-toe/open-heel, below-the-ankle slipper".
ski boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots".
cross-country ski footwear falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots".
snowboard boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots".
skating boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
wrestling boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
boxing boot falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
cycling shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
tennis shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
basketball shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
gym shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
training shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
running shoe falls in the family footwear, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 64, confer "they are designed for a specific sporting activity that generally requires running".

% The kinds of parts and of gaiters (heading 6406; leg warmers: NY N223310)
upper falls in the family footwear part, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Uppers and parts thereof, other than stiffeners".
outer sole falls in the family footwear part, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Outer soles and heels, of rubber or plastics".
heel falls in the family footwear part, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Outer soles and heels, of rubber or plastics".
removable insole falls in the family footwear part, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "removable insoles, heel cushions and similar articles".
heel cushion falls in the family footwear part, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "removable insoles, heel cushions and similar articles".
gaiter falls in the family gaiter, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "gaiters, leggings and similar articles, and parts thereof".
leg warmer falls in the family gaiter, as stated in ruling NY N223310, confer "articles that are designed to cover the whole or part of the leg are more specifically provided for in heading 6406 as gaiters, leggings, and similar articles".
knee warmer falls in the family gaiter, as stated in ruling NY N223310, confer "The applicable subheading for the “leg warmers” and the “knee warmers” will be 6406.90.1510".

% Subheading note 1: the kinds that are sports footwear by name (1(b)), and
% among them the ski footwear of subheadings 6402.12 and 6403.12
ski boot is a kind of ski footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots".
cross-country ski footwear is a kind of ski footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots".
snowboard boot is a kind of ski footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots".
skating boot is a kind of sports footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
wrestling boot is a kind of sports footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
boxing boot is a kind of sports footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".
cycling shoe is a kind of sports footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes".

% Additional U.S. note 2: the athletic footwear the tariff names, and
% running shoes (CN EN to subheading 6404 11 00)
tennis shoe is a kind of athletic footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
basketball shoe is a kind of athletic footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
gym shoe is a kind of athletic footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
training shoe is a kind of athletic footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and the like".
athletic shoe is a kind of athletic footwear, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "covers athletic footwear other than sports footwear".
running shoe is a kind of athletic footwear, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 64, confer "they are designed for a specific sporting activity that generally requires running".

% Kinds that are not "like" the named athletic footwear: a sandal is open
% at the toes or the heel (HQ 963395); a loafer is a slip-on (NY N316838),
% and a slip-on without laces or another secure closure is not athletic
% (NY N255233)
sandal is a kind of non-athletic footwear, as stated in ruling HQ 963395, confer "None of the named exemplars is generally considered to be footwear that is open at the toes or the heel".
thong sandal is a kind of non-athletic footwear, as stated in ruling HQ 963395, confer "Customs generally considers sandals to be casual footwear designed with an emphasis on comfort".
loafer is a kind of non-athletic footwear, as stated in ruling NY N316838, confer "Across the top of the vamp is a decorative band giving the footwear a loafer-type style".
loafer is a kind of non-athletic footwear, as stated in ruling NY N255233, confer "Because the shoe is a slip-on and does not have laces, or another secure form of closure, it is precluded from classification as “athletic” footwear".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The materials of the upper and of the outer sole (notes 3 and 4).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Note 3(a): rubber and plastics, and textile products with a visible
% external layer of rubber or plastics
rubber is of the footwear class rubber-plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Footwear with outer soles and uppers of rubber or plastics".
vulcanized rubber is of the footwear class rubber-plastics,
    as stated in ruling NY N346339, confer "The uppers of all styles are made of vulcanized rubber".
thermoplastic rubber is of the footwear class rubber-plastics,
    as stated in ruling NY N346370, confer "obscured the rubber/plastics underneath".
plastics is of the footwear class rubber-plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Footwear with outer soles and uppers of rubber or plastics".
textile with an external layer of plastics is of the footwear class rubber-plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "the terms \"rubber\" and \"plastics\" include woven fabrics or other textile products with an external layer of rubber or plastics being visible to the naked eye".
textile with an external layer of rubber is of the footwear class rubber-plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "the terms \"rubber\" and \"plastics\" include woven fabrics or other textile products with an external layer of rubber or plastics being visible to the naked eye".
% Note 3(b): leather is the leather of headings 4107 and 4112 to 4114;
% composition leather is a class of its own (CN EN: heading 6405)
leather is of the footwear class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "the term \"leather\" refers to the goods of headings 4107 and 4112 to 4114".
suede leather is of the footwear class leather,
    as stated in ruling NY N252193, confer "outer surface of 85% suede leather".
split leather is of the footwear class leather,
    as stated in ruling NY N251118, confer "a layer of polyurethane coating and a layer of split leather".
composition leather is of the footwear class composition leather,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 64, confer "footwear with furskin uppers or with uppers of composition leather, for example, is excluded from this heading and classified in heading 6405".
% textile materials (CN EN, general note 5: fibres, flock, yarns, fabrics)
textile materials is of the footwear class textile,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "composition leather and uppers of textile materials".
textile flock is of the footwear class textile,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 64, confer "the fibres (for example, textile flock), yarns, fabrics, felts, nonwovens".

% a polymer of Chapter 39 is plastics (Chapter 39 note 1), unless it is
% named as a textile fibre (polyester, nylon...: Section XI)
rule note_64_3a_polymer with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear with outer soles and uppers of rubber or plastics":
a material is of the footwear class rubber-plastics
    if the material is a polymer of a monomer
    and it is not the case that
        the material belongs to a group.

% a textile fibre of Section XI is a textile material
rule note_64_textile_fibre with provenance the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 64,
        confer "the fibres (for example, textile flock), yarns, fabrics, felts, nonwovens":
a material is of the footwear class textile
    if the material belongs to a group.

% Note 4(a): the material of the upper is the constituent material with the
% greatest external surface area, as the ruling states it or from the
% shares of the external surface area it gives
rule note_64_4a_stated with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "The material of the upper shall be taken to be the constituent material having the greatest external surface area":
the upper material of a good is a material
    if the constituent material of the upper of the good is the material.

rule note_64_4a_shares with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "The material of the upper shall be taken to be the constituent material having the greatest external surface area":
the upper material of a good is a material
    if the upper of the good has a number percent of its external surface area of the material
    and it is not the case that
        the constituent material of the upper of the good is an other material
    and it is not the case that
        the upper of the good has an other number percent of its external surface area of a second material
        and the other number > the number.

rule upper_class with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "The material of the upper shall be taken to be the constituent material having the greatest external surface area":
the upper class of a good is a class
    if the upper material of the good is a material
    and the material is of the footwear class the class.

% a material of no class named above (wood, cork, paper, furskin...) is of
% the class "other"
rule upper_class_other with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
the upper class of a good is other
    if the upper material of the good is a material
    and it is not the case that
        the material is of the footwear class a class.

% Note 4(b): the constituent material of the outer sole is the material with
% the greatest surface area in contact with the ground
rule note_64_4b with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "The constituent material of the outer sole shall be taken to be the material having the greatest surface area in contact with":
the outer sole class of a good is a class
    if the constituent material of the outer sole of the good is a material
    and the material is of the footwear class the class.

rule outer_sole_class_other with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
the outer sole class of a good is other
    if the constituent material of the outer sole of the good is a material
    and it is not the case that
        the material is of the footwear class a class.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1), each with the notes that take goods out of it.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% heading 6401: waterproof footwear (Additional U.S. note 3) of rubber or
% plastics whose upper is neither fixed to the sole nor assembled by
% stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing or plugging. Molding and cementing
% are other ways (NY J84062).
rule heading_6401 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Waterproof footwear with outer soles and uppers of rubber or plastics, the uppers of which are neither fixed to the sole nor assembled by stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing, plugging or similar processes":
a good is described by heading 6401
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and the outer sole class of the good is rubber-plastics
    and the upper class of the good is rubber-plastics
    and the good is designed to protect against penetration by water
    and it is not the case that
        the upper of the good is fixed to the sole by a process
        and the process is a process named by heading 6401
    and it is not the case that
        the upper of the good is assembled by a second process
        and the second process is a process named by heading 6401.

stitching is a process named by heading 6401,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "assembled by stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing, plugging or similar processes".
riveting is a process named by heading 6401,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "assembled by stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing, plugging or similar processes".
nailing is a process named by heading 6401,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "assembled by stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing, plugging or similar processes".
screwing is a process named by heading 6401,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "assembled by stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing, plugging or similar processes".
plugging is a process named by heading 6401,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "assembled by stitching, riveting, nailing, screwing, plugging or similar processes".

% heading 6402: other footwear with outer soles and uppers of rubber or
% plastics
rule heading_6402 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Other footwear with outer soles and uppers of rubber or plastics":
a good is described by heading 6402
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and the outer sole class of the good is rubber-plastics
    and the upper class of the good is rubber-plastics.

% heading 6403: uppers of leather; outer soles of rubber, plastics, leather
% or composition leather
rule heading_6403 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear with outer soles of rubber, plastics, leather or composition leather and uppers of leather":
a good is described by heading 6403
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and the outer sole class of the good is a class
    and the class is in [rubber-plastics, leather, composition leather]
    and the upper class of the good is leather.

% heading 6404: uppers of textile materials; the same outer soles
rule heading_6404 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear with outer soles of rubber, plastics, leather or composition leather and uppers of textile materials":
a good is described by heading 6404
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and the outer sole class of the good is a class
    and the class is in [rubber-plastics, leather, composition leather]
    and the upper class of the good is textile.

% heading 6405: other footwear — any footwear whose upper and outer sole
% are known; GRI 3(a) below prefers the headings 6401 to 6404
rule heading_6405 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
a good is described by heading 6405
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and the outer sole class of the good is a class
    and the upper class of the good is an other class.

% heading 6406: parts of footwear, removable insoles, heel cushions,
% gaiters, leggings and similar articles
rule heading_6406 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Parts of footwear (including uppers whether or not attached to soles other than outer soles); removable insoles, heel cushions and similar articles; gaiters, leggings and similar articles, and parts thereof":
a good is described by heading 6406
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [footwear part, gaiter].

% Note 1(a): disposable foot or shoe coverings of flimsy material without
% applied soles are classified by their material
rule note_64_1a with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Disposable foot or shoe coverings of flimsy material (for example, paper, sheeting of plastics) without applied soles":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6401
    and the heading <= 6406
    and the good is a disposable covering of flimsy material without applied soles.

% Note 1(b): footwear of textile material without an outer sole glued,
% sewn or otherwise applied to the upper (Section XI)
rule note_64_1b with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear of textile material, without an outer sole glued, sewn or otherwise affixed or applied to the upper (section XI)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6401
    and the heading <= 6406
    and the good is of textile material without an outer sole applied to the upper.

% Note 1(f): skating boots with ice or roller skates attached (Chapter 95)
rule note_64_1f with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Toy footwear or skating boots with ice or roller skates attached":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6401
    and the heading <= 6406
    and the good has ice or roller skates attached.

% Note 2: pegs, protectors, eyelets, hooks, buckles, ornaments, braid,
% laces, pompons, trimmings and buttons are not parts of heading 6406
rule note_64_2 with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "the term \"parts\" does not include pegs, protectors, eyelets, hooks, buckles, ornaments, braid, laces, pompons or other trimmings":
a good is excluded from heading 6406
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [peg, protector, eyelet, hook, buckle, ornament, braid, lace, shoelace, pompon, trimming, button].

% GRI 3(a): waterproof footwear of 6401 is a more specific description than
% the "other footwear" of rubber or plastics of 6402; 6405 is the
% chapter's residual heading of footwear
rule gri_3a_6401 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading 6401 is more specific than heading 6402.

rule gri_3a_6405 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 6405
    if the heading >= 6401
    and the heading <= 6404.

% Section XI note 1(n): footwear, parts of footwear, gaiters and leggings of
% Chapter 64 are not textiles of Section XI (leg warmers: NY N223310)
rule note_xi_1n with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "(n) Footwear or parts of footwear, gaiters or leggings or similar articles of chapter 64;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 5001
    and the heading <= 6310
    and the other heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6404, 6405, 6406]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Chapter 39 note 2(q): footwear (Section XII) is not of Chapter 39
rule note_39_2q_footwear with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Articles of section XII (for example, footwear, headgear, umbrellas":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3926
    and the other heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6404, 6405, 6406]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Chapter 71 note 3(h): footwear is not of Chapter 71
rule note_71_3h with provenance HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71,
        confer "Footwear, headgear or other articles of chapter 64 or 65;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 7101
    and the heading <= 7118
    and the other heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6404, 6405, 6406]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Chapter 67 note 1(c): footwear is not of Chapter 67
rule note_67_1c with provenance HTSUS Chapter 67, confer "Footwear (chapter 64);":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6701
    and the heading <= 6704
    and the other heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6404, 6405, 6406]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6: what the subheadings read.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule footwear_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6405]
    and the outer sole class of the good is a sole
    and the upper class of the good is an upper
    and the sport class of the good is a sport
    and the strap fixing of the good is a fixing
    and the upper form of the good is a form
    and the toe cap of the good is a cap
    and the height class of the good is a height
    and the subheading in heading the heading for sole the sole with upper the upper with sport the sport with fixing the fixing with form the form with cap the cap with height the height is the code under table footwear.

rule footwear_subheading_6404 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6404 is a code
    if the outer sole class of the good is a sole
    and the sport class of the good is a sport
    and the athletic class of the good is a class
    and the subheading in heading 6404 for sole the sole with sport the sport with athletic class the class is the code under table textile uppers.

rule footwear_subheading_6406 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 6406 is a code
    if the part class of the good is a class
    and the subheading in heading 6406 for the part the class is the code under table footwear parts.

% Subheading note 1: sports footwear is (a) footwear designed for a
% sporting activity with spikes, cleats or the like, or provision for them
% (crampons: HQ H338307), or (b) the boots and shoes the note names
rule sports_footwear_1a with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear which is designed for a sporting activity and has, or has provision for the attachment of spikes, sprigs, cleats, stops, clips, bars or the like":
a good is sports footwear
    if the good is designed for a sporting activity
    and the good has provision for the attachment of spikes or the like.

rule sports_footwear_1b with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes":
a good is sports footwear
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of sports footwear.

rule sports_footwear_ski with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Skating boots, ski-boots and cross-country ski footwear, snowboard boots, wrestling boots, boxing boots and cycling shoes":
a good is sports footwear
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of ski footwear.

rule sport_class_ski with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Ski-boots, cross-country ski footwear and snowboard boots":
the sport class of a good is ski
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of ski footwear.

rule sport_class_sports with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "the expression \"sports footwear\" applies only to":
the sport class of a good is sports
    if the good is sports footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is a kind of ski footwear.

rule sport_class_none with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "the expression \"sports footwear\" applies only to":
the sport class of a good is none
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the good is sports footwear.

% Additional U.S. note 2: athletic footwear other than sports footwear —
% by its kind, or as the office judges its construction and styling (NY
% N253189: "it does resemble athletic footwear in construction and
% styling")
rule athletic_by_kind with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "covers athletic footwear other than sports footwear":
a good is athletic footwear
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of athletic footwear.

rule athletic_by_judgment with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "covers athletic footwear other than sports footwear":
a good is athletic footwear
    if the good is styled as athletic footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is a kind of non-athletic footwear.

rule athletic_class with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "covers athletic footwear other than sports footwear":
the athletic class of a good is athletic
    if the outer sole class of the good is rubber-plastics
    and the good is athletic footwear.

rule athletic_class_other with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "covers athletic footwear other than sports footwear":
the athletic class of a good is other
    if the outer sole class of the good is rubber-plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good is athletic footwear.

% the subheadings of 6404 with an outer sole of leather or composition
% leather do not ask whether the shoe is athletic
rule athletic_class_unread with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear with outer soles of leather or composition leather: 6404.20":
the athletic class of a good is not read
    if the outer sole class of the good is a class
    and it is not the case that
        the class is rubber-plastics.

% the height: covering the knee, covering the ankle (but not the knee), or
% below the ankle
rule height_knee with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Covering the ankle but not covering the knee":
the height class of a good is knee
    if the good covers the knee.

rule height_ankle with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Covering the ankle but not covering the knee":
the height class of a good is ankle
    if the good covers the ankle
    and it is not the case that
        the good covers the knee.

rule height_below with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
the height class of a good is below
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the good covers the ankle
    and it is not the case that
        the good covers the knee.

rule toe_cap_metal with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear incorporating a protective metal toe-cap":
the toe cap of a good is metal
    if the good incorporates a protective metal toe-cap.

rule toe_cap_none with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
the toe cap of a good is none
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the good incorporates a protective metal toe-cap.

rule strap_fixing_plugs with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Footwear with upper straps or thongs assembled to the sole by means of plugs":
the strap fixing of a good is plugs
    if the good has upper straps or thongs assembled to the sole by means of plugs.

rule strap_fixing_none with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
the strap fixing of a good is none
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the good has upper straps or thongs assembled to the sole by means of plugs.

rule upper_form_straps with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "consist of leather straps across the instep and around the big toe":
the upper form of a good is straps
    if the upper of the good consists of straps across the instep and around the big toe.

rule upper_form_other with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other footwear:":
the upper form of a good is other
    if the family of the good is footwear
    and it is not the case that
        the upper of the good consists of straps across the instep and around the big toe.

% the parts of heading 6406: uppers; outer soles and heels of rubber or
% plastics; the rest
rule part_class_upper with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Uppers and parts thereof, other than stiffeners":
the part class of a good is upper
    if the kind of the good is upper.

rule part_class_sole with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64,
        confer "Outer soles and heels, of rubber or plastics":
the part class of a good is sole of rubber-plastics
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [outer sole, heel]
    and the good is wholly or mainly of a material
    and the material is of the footwear class rubber-plastics.

rule part_class_other with provenance HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Other: 6406.90":
the part class of a good is other
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [footwear part, gaiter]
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is upper
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is in [outer sole, heel]
        and the good is wholly or mainly of a material
        and the material is of the footwear class rubber-plastics.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests: goods with the facts a reader writes from a ruling.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% Boots and shoes of rubber or plastics (CBP: the codes the rulings give,
% at six digits)
scenario rubber_and_plastics is:
    % NY N320055: woman's tall boot, upper over 90 percent polyurethane,
    % rubber/plastics lug sole flocked with leather fibres that do not count
    % (note 4(b)), stitched upper -> 6402.91
    the kind of style WP-RYLEEP is boot.
    the constituent material of the upper of style WP-RYLEEP is polyurethane.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of style WP-RYLEEP is rubber.
    the upper of style WP-RYLEEP is assembled by stitching.
    style WP-RYLEEP covers the ankle.
    % NY N313433: duck boot, molded bottom and sewn-on shaft, protective
    % against inclement weather: the stitching keeps it out of 6401 -> 6402.91
    the kind of style SC-HEIDIE is boot.
    the constituent material of the upper of style SC-HEIDIE is polyurethane.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of style SC-HEIDIE is rubber.
    style SC-HEIDIE is designed to protect against penetration by water.
    the upper of style SC-HEIDIE is fixed to the sole by stitching.
    style SC-HEIDIE covers the ankle.
    % NY N323257: children's waterproof boots of rubber or plastic, covering
    % the ankle but not the knee -> 6401.92
    the kind of item 2500100300T5 is rain boot.
    the constituent material of the upper of item 2500100300T5 is plastics.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of item 2500100300T5 is rubber.
    item 2500100300T5 is designed to protect against penetration by water.
    item 2500100300T5 covers the ankle.
    % NY N346339: children's rain boots, uppers of vulcanized rubber, outsole
    % rubber with a dusting of leather flocking (a similar attachment) -> 6401.92
    the kind of style K1367 is rain boot.
    the constituent material of the upper of style K1367 is vulcanized rubber.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of style K1367 is rubber.
    style K1367 is designed to protect against penetration by water.
    style K1367 covers the ankle.
    % NY N172458: "Ribbon Flip Flop", PVC strap upper plugged into a
    % polyethylene sole -> 6402.20
    the kind of the ribbon flip flop is thong sandal.
    the constituent material of the upper of the ribbon flip flop is polyvinyl chloride.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of the ribbon flip flop is polyethylene.
    the ribbon flip flop has upper straps or thongs assembled to the sole by means of plugs.
    % HQ H338307: mountaineering boots, upper 88.59 percent rubber/plastics,
    % crampon compatible: sports footwear -> 6402.19
    the kind of the winter reboot is boot.
    the upper of the winter reboot has 88.59 percent of its external surface area of plastics.
    the upper of the winter reboot has 11.41 percent of its external surface area of textile materials.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of the winter reboot is rubber.
    the winter reboot covers the ankle.
    the winter reboot is designed for a sporting activity.
    the winter reboot has provision for the attachment of spikes or the like.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style WP-RYLEEP is 6402.91", "the subheading of style SC-HEIDIE is 6402.91", "the subheading of item 2500100300T5 is 6401.92", "the subheading of style K1367 is 6401.92", "the subheading of the ribbon flip flop is 6402.20", "the subheading of the winter reboot is 6402.19"].

% Uppers of leather, of textile and of other materials
scenario leather_and_textile is:
    % NY J84976: men's lace-up shoes with leather uppers and rubber/plastic
    % soles, below the ankle -> 6403.99
    the kind of style BM5027 is shoe.
    the constituent material of the upper of style BM5027 is leather.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of style BM5027 is rubber.
    % NY N274653: mule-type sandal, upper 69.42 percent leather and 30.58
    % percent PU -> 6403.99
